# =============================================================================
# gtVdB parameters file  (Oracle-style: flat KEY=VALUE, all-uppercase keys)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this to one of the locations below and edit as needed:
#   * $GTV_PARAMS_FILE            (explicit path, highest precedence)
#   * ./gtvdb.params              (current working directory)
#   * <exe-dir>/gtvdb.params      (next to the gtv binary)
#   * /etc/gtvdb/gtvdb.params     (Unix) | C:\ProgramData\gtvdb\gtvdb.params (Win)
#
# Syntax
#   * # and -- start a comment; blank lines are ignored.
#   * KEY=VALUE or KEY VALUE (whitespace also accepted).
#   * Keys are case-insensitive; values are not.
#   * Sizes accept binary suffixes K/M/G/T (optional trailing B): 16000M = 16000 MiB.
#   * Fractions: SYSTEM:0.5 = half of system RAM; TARGET:0.5 = half of
#     MEMORY_TARGET; DEVICE:0.8 = 80% of the CUDA device VRAM.
#   * Keywords AUTO / SYSTEM / ON / OFF / TRUE / FALSE accepted where sensible.
#
# Environment overrides (highest priority) use GTV_PARAM_<KEY>, e.g.
#   export GTV_PARAM_MEMORY_TARGET=32000M
# Other long-standing env knobs are still honoured: GTV_SPILL_DIR,
# GTV_TARGET_PARTITIONS, GTV_BATCH_SIZE.
# =============================================================================

# --- Memory -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Total memory gtVdB may allocate. Default: half of system physical RAM.
# Set explicitly to cap the DataFusion memory pool (only mounted when explicit).
MEMORY_TARGET=SYSTEM:0.5

# Resident-in-memory object area (objects kept hot). Default: half of
# MEMORY_TARGET. Must not exceed MEMORY_TARGET.
MEMORY_OBJ_AREA=TARGET:0.5

# --- CUDA / GPU -------------------------------------------------------------
# OFF  = never use the GPU.
# AUTO = use the GPU only when a device is detectable (default).
# ON   = require a device; gtVdB fails to start if none is present.
CUDA_MODE=AUTO

# VRAM budget gtVdB may use. Default: 80% of device VRAM (DEVICE:0.8).
# Use a concrete size (e.g. 6000M) to pin it.
CUDA_VRAM=DEVICE:0.8

# Device ordinal when multiple GPUs are present.
CUDA_DEVICE=0

# --- Device cache (the GPU-resident working set) ----------------------------
# What happens to a corpus / right-side series once it is uploaded:
#   OFF    = never keep a device copy; every operation runs on the host.
#   SHADOW = run on the host, but keep the residency ledger and hit/miss
#            accounting as if the cache were live. Use this to size VRAM before
#            buying a GPU: `.accel` reports the hit ratio and the upload bytes a
#            device would have saved.
#   ON     = keep the device copy and run there when it fits (default).
# Accommodating an oversized dataset is never fatal: it is declined and that one
# operation runs on the host, while everything else keeps its device copy.
ACCEL_CACHE=ON

# Pending host->device delta that triggers one batched upload. Default: 25% of
# CUDA_VRAM. Until then, queries read the resident prefix from the device and the
# un-synced tail from the host, so an append never stalls or invalidates a query.
# Accepts AUTO (the 25% default) or a concrete size:
# ACCEL_SYNC_THRESHOLD=512M

# Seconds after the last upload at which pending delta is applied even if the
# byte threshold was not reached. 0 = apply on every batch boundary.
ACCEL_SYNC_INTERVAL=5

# Half-life (seconds) of a resident block's access heat. Heat = decayed
# frequency, used for admission and eviction: a proven-hot corpus is not
# displaced by a one-shot scan, and a declined corpus can still earn its way
# back in after a few queries. 0 disables heat and restores pure LRU.
ACCEL_HEAT_HALF_LIFE=30

# --- Query dialect ----------------------------------------------------------
# SQL = standard DataFusion SQL (default). Q = native q dialect (needs the
# quantum/q extension; falls back to SQL with a warning if unavailable).
DEFAULT_MODE=SQL

# --- Runtime / deployment tuning -------------------------------------------
# Log verbosity: ERROR | WARN | INFO | DEBUG | TRACE. Surfaces via RUST_LOG.
LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# Spill directory for large sorts/joins. GTV_SPILL_DIR env wins if set.
# SPILL_DIR=/var/lib/gtv/spill

# Worker thread count (parallelism). AUTO => GTV_TARGET_PARTITIONS or CPU count.
# WORKER_THREADS=AUTO

# Directories used by deployment layouts (read by tooling; see docs).
# DATA_DIR=./data
# CATALOG_DIR=./catalog

# Optional telemetry toggle.
TELEMETRY=FALSE
